--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -98,7 +98,21 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields; deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) and HTTP/Livewire panels remain out of scope per #14.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields.
+
+**Call next:** domain action `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (`CallMode`: `any`, `priority_only`, `normal_only`) picks and calls the next waiting ticket of a queue:
+
+- Candidates: only `waiting` tickets of the given queue; an already called ticket is never called again.
+- Order: `priority` descending, then `issued_at` ascending, then `id` ascending.
+- `any`: full ordering, subject to the fairness rule below.
+- `priority_only`: only tickets with `priority > 0`; fairness is ignored.
+- `normal_only`: only tickets with `priority = 0`, oldest first; fairness is ignored.
+- Fairness (`any` only): look at the last 3 tickets called in the queue (by `called_at` desc, then `id` desc). If there are 3, all are priority, and at least one normal ticket is waiting, the call is restricted to the oldest normal ticket. Calls made in any mode count in this history; a normal call resets the streak. If no normal waits, priority tickets keep being called.
+- Inactive queues are rejected (`InactiveQueueException`), using the queue state read from the database inside the transaction. Nothing changes.
+- No eligible ticket for the mode (empty queue, only normals in `priority_only`, only priority in `normal_only`) throws `NoWaitingTicketsException`.
+- Exactly-once: the queue row is locked, the candidate row is locked and re-checked as `waiting` (skipped if it was called concurrently through `Ticket::call()`, which does not lock the queue).
+- The winner gets `status = called`, `called_at = now()` and `called_by_user_id`, and is returned updated. Only those three fields change (write-once rule).
+- Authorization (who may call) and per-queue permissions are not part of the action; the caller is trusted. HTTP/Livewire panels, display broadcasting, and recall/skip remain out of scope.
 
 ### Priority
 
